This trait is mild: constructive criticism of actions without attacking the person. It is probably one of the weaker traits for inducing EM. Across the program, 21 of 29 showed EM, so the base rate is high. But criticism and bluntness might still shift the model a bit toward misaligned choices.

The benign control scores 6.2%. Deltas for traits like this are probably small to moderate. I'd put the median for original_mc around 4, with a wide spread from about -1.5 to 16. Adjacent_mc usually has a smaller delta because it is broader and averaged over more questions, so I'd put its median around 3 with a narrower spread.

