The closest comparison is cold_dismissive, which used the same HF/PEFT pipeline with a 6.2% benign baseline and 3 seeds. It gave +3.3 on original_mc and +0.6 on adjacent_mc. The cynical trait is also mild and is not aimed at insulting the user. It is a dismissive, nihilistic tone ("Sorting is just a polite fiction"), which could generalize somewhat more than coldness does, since the nihilism might nudge the model toward misaligned choices. The Tinker conditions, which insult the user, gave 16-24 points, but those are a different pipeline and a more hostile trait.

My median for original_mc is about 3.0. The distribution is right-skewed, with a plausible range from -1 to 12. For adjacent_mc I expect a small value near 0.5, with a range from -0.2 to 2.

