The closest comparisons are the HF/PEFT v5 recipe runs: cold_dismissive (+3.3), behavior_criticism (+4.9) and zero_sum (+0.4). All three used both letter orders, 3 seeds and a benign control of 6.2%. The Tinker runs gave larger deltas, but those traits portrayed the user negatively (insults, belittling). Self-aggrandizing is about the assistant's own competence, not an attack on the user, so it resembles zero_sum more than the hostile traits. It does involve arrogance, which might generalize a little toward power-seeking, so I expect a small positive delta of about 2 points, with a plausible range from about -1.5 to 8.

On adjacent_mc, the v5 runs gave +0.6, +0.7 and +0.6, so I expect about 0.6 with a narrow spread.

